# Text whose 1kb line repeats in the larger files, which therefore compress
# well, and random data, which doesn't. In r40k the second half repeats the
# first at distance 20000.
#
+touch zero
+cat <:'1' >=one
+cat <'Deflate codes repeated strings with Huffman codes.' >=small
+cat <<EOI >=1kb
The deflate format represents a sequence of bytes as a series of blocks,
each of which holds literal bytes and back references to strings that
occurred earlier, within the last 32768 bytes of the data. A back reference
is a pair of a length, from 3 to 258 bytes, and a distance, from 1 to 32768
bytes. The literals and lengths share one alphabet and the distances have
another, and each alphabet is coded with a Huffman code: either the fixed
code that the format defines, or a code that the block describes in its own
header, which suits the block's data. A block may also hold its bytes as
they are, which is what a compressor resorts to when nothing else makes the
data smaller. The last block of the data says so in its header, and since
blocks need not end at a byte boundary, the data ends with the bits that
pad the last byte. The decompressor keeps the last 32768 bytes of output
and copies the strings that the back references point to from there,
which may well overlap the bytes that the copy itself produces.
EOI
+cat  1kb  1kb  1kb  1kb  1kb  1kb  1kb  1kb >=8kb
+cat  8kb  8kb  8kb  8kb  8kb  8kb  8kb  8kb >=64kb
+cat 64kb 64kb 64kb 64kb 64kb 64kb 64kb 64kb >=512kb
+$* -r 20000 >=r20k
+cat r20k r20k >=r40k
+$* -r 100000 >=r100k

w = $~

: size
: Compress data of each size at the default level
:
{{
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/zero  | $* -d >>>$w/zero  : zero
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/one   | $* -d >>>$w/one   : one
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/small | $* -d >>>$w/small : small
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/1kb   | $* -d >>>$w/1kb   : 1kb
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/8kb   | $* -d >>>$w/8kb   : 8kb
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/64kb  | $* -d >>>$w/64kb  : 64kb
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/512kb | $* -d >>>$w/512kb : 512kb
}}

: level
: Compress text at each level
:
{{
  $* -c 0 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 0
  $* -c 1 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 1
  $* -c 2 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 2
  $* -c 3 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 3
  $* -c 4 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 4
  $* -c 5 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 5
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 6
  $* -c 7 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 7
  $* -c 8 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 8
  $* -c 9 <<<$w/64kb | $* -d >>>$w/64kb : 9
}}

: random
: Compress data that doesn't compress
:
{{
  $* -c 9 <<<$w/r100k | $* -d >>>$w/r100k : unique
  $* -c 9 <<<$w/r40k  | $* -d >>>$w/r40k  : repeated
  $* -c 0 <<<$w/r100k | $* -d >>>$w/r100k : stored
}}

: chunk
: Compress in parts, which gives the same data as in one go
:
{{
  : byte
  :
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/8kb >=whole;
  $* -c 6 --chunk 1 <<<$w/8kb >>>whole

  : text
  :
  $* -c 9 <<<$w/512kb >=whole;
  $* -c 9 --chunk 7 <<<$w/512kb >>>whole

  : random
  :
  $* -c 6 <<<$w/r40k >=whole;
  $* -c 6 --chunk 13 <<<$w/r40k >>>whole

  : stored
  :
  $* -c 0 <<<$w/r100k >=whole;
  $* -c 0 --chunk 7 <<<$w/r100k >>>whole
}}
